Done: PR #561 is merged and released. https://github.com/valentinyeo/postbox/pull/561

**Final state**
- Merged 18:40Z as squash commit `e4faa39` on `main`; branch `soft-3105-read-mark-jump` deleted.
- Release `v0.9.541` built from that commit: success (https://github.com/valentinyeo/postbox/actions/runs/45241231268).
- Every check green at the merged head `83fd83e`: `ci`, `tdlib`, `windows-smoke`, `no-comments`, `unfurl-verification`, `private-markers`, `secret-scan`, `pr-title`, `verify-verdict`, plus `verify (read-ticks)`, `verify (media-fit)`, `caption-verification`.

**Failures, cause, fix**
1. `verify (read-ticks, true)` on the old head: the journey waited 90s for "read mark shown and repainted". The single Read mark no longer exists. Fixed by the ticks commit `8d51c09`: per-message status from `DeliveredTo`/`ReadBy`, rewritten journey that counts grey and blue pixels in each bubble's bottom-right.
2. `verify (read-ticks, true)` on `b0e2857`: timed out at "the newest hold message reports read". The fake hub's `ReadTicksHandler` only overrode `do_GET`, so `/fixture/ticks/read` published no event and the app never refetched. Fixed in `83fd83e` (own SSE stream in the fixture).
3. `caption-verification`: "media-fit: calibration must show eight separate M glyphs". The ticks draw inside the own bubble and added a ninth ink run to the word-step scan. Fixed in `b0e2857`: the measured band stops 12px above the bubble bottom in `media-fit.cs` and in `check-media-fit-evidence.py`, where the bubble's 10px bottom pad keeps text out.
4. `pr-title`: my first body edit dropped the `Revert:` line. Added `Revert: none, ...`. Note `gh pr edit` itself fails here (see fault 1), so I patched title and body through `gh api PATCH`.
5. The burst of instant "fail 0s" entries (`plan`, `native-tests`, `candidate`, `planted`) were cancelled jobs from superseded runs, not failures. Editing the PR body starts a second verify-wazig run that cancels the first. They passed on the next full run.

**What Valentin sees now**: one grey tick for sent, two grey for delivered, two blue for read, inside every own bubble. Slack and Signal groups show none. A receipt cannot move the chat, because the ticks never change a row's height. The Windows journey proved it on the real binary: pixels counted per chat, and the hold bubble kept its height, bottom edge and scroll position when delivered turned blue.

**Faults for the orchestrator**
1. Shared GitHub tooling: `gh pr edit` exits 1 with `GraphQL: Projects (classic) is being deprecated ...` and applies nothing. Route to the gh wrapper owner.
2. Worker repo board/view: `tools/test_verify_journeys.py` fails locally with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'real_size_seed'` for the `real-size` fixture. Pre-existing and sandbox-only, it passes in CI. Already flagged by the earlier worker.
3. Coordination: a second agent pushed `83fd83e` onto this branch while I was watching CI. Two workers on one ticket can overwrite each other; worth one worker per PR.
4. No Hypertask board login here, so SOFT-3129, SOFT-3105 and SOFT-2913 are not moved to Done. The orchestrator files that.

Next action: install Postbox `v0.9.541` and open a WhatsApp chat to see the ticks.
